# WayExpand evdev capture backend (--source=evdev) reads /dev/input/event*
# directly. Most systemd-based distributions already grant GROUP="input"
# MODE="0660" to input devices via their own default rules (see
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/50-udev-default.rules); this file only reasserts
# that same default explicitly for keyboard event nodes, so WayExpand does
# not silently depend on it being present. It does not grant anything
# beyond what a standard systemd installation already grants members of
# the `input` group.
#
# This is the current legacy/simple permission model. It is installed by
# scripts/install-evdev-permissions.sh, which also adds the
# invoking user to the `input` group. Read SECURITY.md for what that
# membership grants before enabling --source=evdev: it lets a process read
# every keystroke typed on this system, in any session, not only ones
# passed to WayExpand's own matcher. See docs/EVDEV_ACCESS_DESIGN.md for the
# active-seat ACL and device-broker investigation.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
